  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Ground floor rear extension to replace existing kitchen/conservatory extensions. First floor rear extension and front extension to extend bedrooms. External alterations",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposal, by reason of the site being located within an area of land liable to\r\nflooding and the lack of a comprehensive Flood Risk Assessment, due to a lack\r\nof up to date flood maps/data, has failed to demonstrate that the proposed\r\ndevelopment would not exacerbate the risk of flooding within the site or\r\nincrease the risk and consequences of flooding elsewhere, contrary to the\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies SI12 and SI13 of The London\r\nPlan (2021), Core Policy CS1.U of Harrow Core Strategy (2012) and Policies DM9\r\nand DM10 of the Harrow Development Management Polices Local Plan (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposed patio/terraced decking, by virtue\r\nof its height and proximity to the boundary shared with No. 28 Murray Crescent,\r\nwould result an unreasonable degree of increased overlooking and a loss of\r\nprivacy to No. 28 Murray Crescent. The proposal is therefore contrary to the\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3.D(7) of the London Plan\r\n(2021), policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan\r\n(2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design\r\nGuide (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
